VK: find physical devices through vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices, not device groups.

NRI dropped mGPU support in v1.124 (7bb624d), but DeviceVK::Create and the adapter enumeration
(UpdateAdaptersVK) still list physical devices through vkEnumeratePhysicalDeviceGroups and then use
only "physicalDevices[0]" of each group: a device is created on one physical device, without
VkDeviceGroupDeviceCreateInfo. The groups add nothing but the subset-allocation warning, which
describes a multi-device group NRI no longer creates.

Group-only enumeration breaks overlay layers that track physical devices from
vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices. RivaTuner Statistics Server's implicit VK_LAYER_RTSS (bundled with MSI
Afterburner; the overlay of CapFrameX and HWiNFO too) maps each physical device to its instance from
that call and uses the map when its overlay initialises at the first vkQueuePresentKHR. Measured on
v191, RTSS 7.3.5, NVIDIA RTX 4070 SUPER: every NRI-created Vulkan device that presents dies with
0xC0000409 inside the first QueuePresent, with NRI validation and the Khronos layer each on or off,
hidden or shown window (16 runs); with DISABLE_RTSS_LAYER=1, or after one extra
vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices on NRI's instance, each run presents 120 frames. Engines that call
vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices themselves never see it; the 7.3.7 release notes name no such fix.

This enumerates physical devices in both places, the same number of calls, and drops the group
warning. One difference on hardware with linked GPUs (a group of more than one physical device):
each physical device is listed instead of the group's first; the adapter list still merges entries
with the same uid, and device creation still takes the first match.

